  "question": {
    "text": "If the middle term in the expansion of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>10</mn></msup></math> is equal to <math><mn>7</mn><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> then the number of values of <math><mi>x</mi></math> in <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>There are <math><mn>11</mn></math> terms in the expansion <math><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> term is the middle term</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mn>10</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msup><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msup></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>5</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mn>10</mn></mmultiscripts><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>63</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>63</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>×</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, there are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
